# Test: daemon start refuses fib kernel alone (without fib vpp) under interface backend vpp.
# Question: does `ze start` on a file with `interface backend vpp` and
#           `fib kernel` alone (no `fib vpp` block) exit 1 before any plugin
#           starts, naming `fib kernel` and `set fib vpp`?
#           A unit test exercises the verdict over synthetic registrations;
#           only a real daemon start proves the composition-root `fib-kernel`
#           and `fib-vpp` registrations refuse boot ahead of plugin start.
# VALIDATES: spec-dataplane-compatibility-guard AC-14 (P-1b at start) --
#            a host-side FIB writer of another plane alone under VPP leaves
#            VPP's FIB with no route and is refused at daemon start.
# PREVENTS: a VPP daemon booting with only `fib kernel` and forwarding traffic
#           with an empty VPP FIB.

option=needs-build-tag:value=ze_vpp:state=present

stdin=ze-bgp:refused=config-plugin-verify:terminator=EOF_CONF
interface {
	backend vpp;
}
fib {
	kernel {
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stderr:contains=error: load config:
expect=stderr:contains=fib kernel
expect=stderr:contains=set fib vpp
reject=stderr:contains=interface backend loaded
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
